{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1780542842,"nonce":"MJVtZ3YPTxAqNeosrwF/Gc7tiSs=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABE0qMKw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/145#issuecomment-4618619947"},"message":"## Field instance from #211 (2026-06-03) — bridge Starlink dropout, bag-verified\n\nConcrete motivating case for this issue. Transiting under the Little Harbour bridge on manual control, the Starlink path was occluded by the span and **command/control was lost for ~18 s**, during which the boat drifted uncontrolled near the pilings.\n\n**Evidence (cross-source, `/bizzy/piloting_mode/manual/helm`):** operator bag = sent, boat bag = received.\n- Healthy through 16:55:34; **16:55:36–16:55:54 (~18 s) operator sending continuously, boat received 0** → Starlink occlusion; recovered 16:55:56.\n- During the dropout `/bizzy/mavros/rc/out` went neutral/erratic (thrust ~1500/1065, steering swinging) → no command hold → ~18 s drift.\n- **Correction:** the field log's \"lost Starlink ~17:15 / pushed back\" and a first-pass \"875 s outage\" were both wrong — that 875 s was the operator off-manual (sent *and* received both idle). Real outage ≈ 18 s.\n\n**Refined approach (Roland, 2026-06-03):** not a bonded link — a **third independently-addressable link** (cell-based VPN with its own address space, exactly like the existing WiFi vs VPN address spaces we select between), with **udp_bridge carrying only the essentials** (command / heartbeat / safety-critical telemetry) over the cell path. Keeps the high-bandwidth stream on Starlink, while control survives Starlink occlusion via the separately-addressed cell channel — and stays under the low-bandwidth threshold that keeps cell reliable (per this issue's DPI hypothesis).\n\nSecondary, smaller: a comms-loss **station-keep/hold failsafe** so an *uncovered* dropout doesn't drift near hazards — but the essentials-on-cell channel is the primary fix.\n\nRelated: #68 (drop costmap from bridge), #130 (OTH), #152 (rear cam over VPN). Data: `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-06-03/`.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}